WEBVTT

00:43.626 --> 00:48.381
DOONA!

02:05.458 --> 02:10.255
EPISODE 1
AN UNEXPECTED TWIST

02:15.760 --> 02:19.639
KOOK'S SEAFOOD HOUSE

02:30.024 --> 02:31.901
KOOK'S SEAFOOD HOUSE
CEO KOOK SU-JIN

02:33.278 --> 02:35.446
I've had business cards made.

02:38.074 --> 02:40.535
I'm jealous. You're already a CEO at 21.

02:40.618 --> 02:43.037
Now that you're the boss,
get to work earlier.

02:43.121 --> 02:45.415
The grocery boxes are too heavy
for my mom to carry.

02:45.498 --> 02:48.459
You're that worried about your mom,
but you're running off to Seoul?

02:49.127 --> 02:51.629
The commute has always been a problem.

02:51.713 --> 02:53.631
And with Won-yeong now
out of the hospital,

02:54.632 --> 02:57.343
I figured it'd be better
to use the commute time productively.

02:59.387 --> 03:00.513
Hey, Kooksu.

03:01.764 --> 03:02.765
Thank you.

03:03.349 --> 03:04.767
Take care of my mom for me.

03:04.851 --> 03:06.895
Don't even worry about it, doofus.

03:10.523 --> 03:14.194
If, by any chance,
you happen to see Doona in Seoul,

03:14.277 --> 03:15.820
you have got to call me, okay?

03:15.904 --> 03:18.072
Yeah, right. As if.

03:18.156 --> 03:20.950
WHEN THE ANSWERS INCLUDE
VERBS AND NON-VERBS

03:26.539 --> 03:27.540
I'm sorry.

04:05.286 --> 04:06.871
AEIHERUMUH
LOVE AND DO WHAT YOU WILL

04:22.220 --> 04:23.346
Hello.

05:06.889 --> 05:07.724
It's open.

05:21.571 --> 05:22.780
Excuse me.

05:23.990 --> 05:25.575
Have we met before?

05:29.996 --> 05:30.913
Maybe not.

05:32.123 --> 05:34.959
I must have mistaken you for someone else.
You looked familiar.

05:36.836 --> 05:37.754
I'm sorry.

05:38.755 --> 05:41.341
Oh! I'm just moving in
on the second floor.

05:41.424 --> 05:44.093
I hope we can get along.
It's my first time living on my own.

06:04.947 --> 06:06.908
AUTHORIZED PERSONNEL ONLY
PLEASE KNOCK

06:12.538 --> 06:14.499
Hello, I'm Lee Won-jun. I'm just moving--

06:14.582 --> 06:16.876
Please refer to this notice.

06:17.460 --> 06:18.795
HOUSE RULES

06:18.878 --> 06:20.671
In particular, Clause Seven. Laundry.

06:22.298 --> 06:25.676
I recommend that you use the rooftop
for your laundry.

06:30.765 --> 06:31.599
I mean, yes.

06:42.944 --> 06:45.446
- Newbie?
- Hello, I'm--

06:45.530 --> 06:46.989
Senior year, Psychology.

06:48.074 --> 06:50.201
Taek, Taek, Yun-taek.

06:51.244 --> 06:52.537
Seo Yun-taek, that's me.

06:53.204 --> 06:56.624
Right, I'm Lee Won-jun.
Sophomore, Civil Engineering.

06:56.707 --> 06:59.377
There is absolutely nothing
to be worried about.

06:59.877 --> 07:01.421
Here, you can just be yourself.

07:01.504 --> 07:02.797
Live free.

07:03.423 --> 07:04.257
Okay?

07:04.340 --> 07:05.174
Yes.

07:57.268 --> 07:58.227
No!

07:58.311 --> 07:59.270
Oh no!

08:07.278 --> 08:08.279
What the heck?!

08:27.882 --> 08:28.758
There.

08:35.348 --> 08:36.265
Perfect.

08:42.438 --> 08:43.981
"Organic pumpkin juice."

08:58.412 --> 09:00.998
MINSONG NATIONAL UNIVERSITY
CIVIL ENGINEERING TOP SCHOLAR

09:01.082 --> 09:04.335
PRIVATE TUITION

09:39.036 --> 09:40.871
KOREAN TUTOR
MINSONG KOR LIT FRESHMAN

09:41.706 --> 09:43.165
Look, there are still some left.

09:44.292 --> 09:45.543
Oh, thank God.

09:46.168 --> 09:47.420
- Here.
- Thanks.

09:49.297 --> 09:50.715
Hey, did you see his hoodie?

09:51.215 --> 09:52.508
He must be a total fanboy.

09:52.592 --> 09:54.093
Why would he wear that in public?

09:54.176 --> 09:56.262
- That's actually kinda adorable.
- Agreed.

10:40.973 --> 10:43.684
THERE'S A STALKER ON THE SECOND FLOOR

11:19.679 --> 11:20.721
KOOK SU-JIN

11:21.681 --> 11:22.556
Hey, CEO Kook.

11:22.640 --> 11:24.600
Hey, bro.

11:24.684 --> 11:26.894
Get ready to kiss
your big bro's feet, bro.

11:26.977 --> 11:28.104
Kiss your feet?

11:29.271 --> 11:31.816
Someone's paying 800,000 won a month?

11:31.899 --> 11:33.317
Sick, isn't it?

11:33.401 --> 11:35.194
And that's just for math.

11:35.277 --> 11:36.404
Freaking sweet!

11:36.487 --> 11:38.155
Wow, that's insane!

11:38.239 --> 11:41.075
That will cover my rent
and living expenses.

11:41.158 --> 11:43.244
CEO Kook, I don't know how to thank you.

11:43.327 --> 11:45.579
Please pass my thanks on to your mom too.

11:45.663 --> 11:47.665
How's the house? Is it okay?

11:47.748 --> 11:51.711
Screaming out so loud…

11:51.794 --> 11:53.045
What?

11:53.129 --> 11:55.131
I can't hear you.
Turn the music down a bit.

11:55.214 --> 11:57.007
Dream Sweet Lee Doona!

11:57.091 --> 11:58.551
I love you forever!

11:58.634 --> 12:01.512
This is how much I love Doona!

12:01.595 --> 12:03.639
Jeez, what the hell?

12:03.723 --> 12:06.100
Didn't you throw out their albums
and quit being a fan?

12:07.268 --> 12:10.354
It's not that easy to give up
something you love so much.

12:10.438 --> 12:12.523
Oh, hey, speaking of which,

12:12.606 --> 12:15.276
give me back the hoodie
I gave you last time.

12:15.776 --> 12:19.196
It's limited edition merch.
There won't be any new Doona merch.

12:19.280 --> 12:20.698
Merch?

12:21.198 --> 12:23.117
I thought it was my birthday present.

12:25.077 --> 12:26.078
Oh no!

12:26.162 --> 12:28.247
I was wearing it all day yesterday!

12:28.330 --> 12:30.583
What? Who wears merch!

12:30.666 --> 12:33.836
READ
THERE'S A STALKER ON THE SECOND FLOOR

12:43.137 --> 12:45.848
I got this, 800,000

12:46.807 --> 12:49.435
Per subject, 800,000

12:50.060 --> 12:53.355
I'll sneak into your dreams

12:53.439 --> 12:54.315
I stab

12:54.398 --> 12:55.483
I want…

13:01.614 --> 13:02.782
Are you messing with me?

13:06.619 --> 13:07.453
I remember now.

13:10.873 --> 13:12.917
You're Lee Doona, right? Dream Sweet.

13:13.000 --> 13:14.627
It's finally come to me.

13:15.795 --> 13:17.213
It's finally come to you. Really?

13:17.296 --> 13:19.882
I'm sorry? I didn't quite catch that.
What did you…

13:23.594 --> 13:25.679
Give the crappy acting a rest.

13:29.183 --> 13:31.352
Are you insane? I could have gotten hurt!

13:32.436 --> 13:33.395
But you didn't.

13:34.188 --> 13:35.356
What?

13:35.439 --> 13:36.982
How did you know I live here?

13:37.066 --> 13:38.150
I didn't.

13:39.026 --> 13:40.861
Did you put up a spycam or something?

13:42.112 --> 13:43.656
What is it you want to see so much

13:44.990 --> 13:46.909
that you'd even move here to stalk me?

13:47.409 --> 13:49.620
I'm really not a stalker.

13:49.703 --> 13:52.665
My friend is a fan of yours
so you looked familiar. That's why--

13:54.458 --> 13:56.669
I'm sorry. I won't look at you again.

14:02.591 --> 14:03.801
But you know what?

14:04.552 --> 14:06.178
I like TWICE.

14:15.729 --> 14:17.273
MOM

14:18.440 --> 14:19.817
DECLINE

14:26.073 --> 14:29.493
In terms of math, I can confidently say
that you won't find a better tutor.

14:29.577 --> 14:32.329
I have expertise
due to extensive tutoring experience.

14:32.955 --> 14:34.248
I can say that for certain.

14:35.916 --> 14:38.627
You're earnest and polite. I like that.

14:40.087 --> 14:43.090
Does that mean I can start next week?

14:43.966 --> 14:44.925
Yes.

14:47.845 --> 14:49.263
- Mr. Lee!
- Yes?

14:50.723 --> 14:53.517
Well, you forgot this.

14:53.601 --> 14:55.352
Oh. Thank you.

15:11.452 --> 15:13.203
MATH TUITION

15:14.371 --> 15:15.915
Are you looking for a tutor--

15:18.626 --> 15:20.002
Won-jun!

15:26.675 --> 15:28.969
It's been a while, Jin-ju.

15:38.687 --> 15:41.106
I didn't recognize you
because of the short hair.

15:41.190 --> 15:44.026
Really? I've had this
for more than a year now.

15:46.779 --> 15:47.613
Exactly.

15:49.990 --> 15:51.659
It's been a long time, hasn't it?

15:56.163 --> 15:57.706
That hairstyle suits you too.

15:58.749 --> 16:01.126
Where do you live?
Are you still commuting?

16:01.210 --> 16:04.213
Just until last semester.
I'm in a nearby house share now.

16:07.049 --> 16:09.510
That's a shame.
I thought we could commute together.

16:10.427 --> 16:13.931
Five hours on the road
is going to be so tedious.

16:14.014 --> 16:15.349
What do you mean?

16:15.891 --> 16:17.601
I'm at Minsong now too.

16:20.020 --> 16:23.440
Come on, I got in on my second attempt.
Aren't you going to congratulate me?

16:24.233 --> 16:25.526
Oh. Here.

16:25.609 --> 16:26.443
Cheers!

16:31.532 --> 16:32.616
Wow.

16:40.958 --> 16:41.792
It's so cold.

16:46.588 --> 16:48.841
- Here.
- Oh, you don't have to.

16:48.924 --> 16:51.135
Take it. It's cold. And it's snowing.

16:52.636 --> 16:54.138
All right, then. Thank you.

16:58.434 --> 16:59.685
You're still so sweet.

17:05.941 --> 17:06.775
This is me.

17:10.529 --> 17:11.905
And this is me.

17:13.032 --> 17:14.575
So that's who my competitor was.

17:14.658 --> 17:16.410
We've always been competitors.

17:16.493 --> 17:18.162
Only I've never beaten you.

17:27.588 --> 17:30.549
Anyhow, let's hang out often
now that we're in the same school.

17:31.091 --> 17:31.925
Sure.

17:35.387 --> 17:36.597
My bus is here.

17:38.015 --> 17:38.974
See you later.

18:07.795 --> 18:10.172
KOREAN TUITION FOR CSAT
MINSONG KOR LIT FRESHMAN

18:55.801 --> 18:57.678
Is she all right in this cold?

19:25.330 --> 19:26.748
- You!
- Yes?

19:35.674 --> 19:37.009
Don't sing.

19:38.302 --> 19:39.845
You really suck at it.

19:42.556 --> 19:44.975
If you sing that song around me
one more time,

19:45.475 --> 19:47.603
I'll smash your head in.

19:47.686 --> 19:48.979
Smash what?

19:58.655 --> 19:59.698
Hey.

19:59.781 --> 20:01.366
Are you okay? Can you hear me?

20:09.374 --> 20:12.294
Oh, hi. I'm at 21 Minsongdae-gil.

20:12.377 --> 20:14.087
Someone's collapsed and is unconscious.

20:14.880 --> 20:16.590
I think you should get here quickly.

20:16.673 --> 20:18.717
Could you please hurry?

20:19.343 --> 20:20.510
Yes.

20:48.247 --> 20:49.665
JOB HUNTING STUDY GROUP

20:49.748 --> 20:52.501
Is this only applicable to seniors?

20:54.211 --> 20:55.045
Hey.

20:56.880 --> 20:57.714
You're awake.

20:57.798 --> 20:59.216
You're in the hospital.

21:00.926 --> 21:03.804
Oh, the nurse was asking
about your guardian.

21:06.056 --> 21:07.182
I don't have one.

21:12.479 --> 21:14.398
You should call your family…

21:15.399 --> 21:16.650
I said I don't have one.

21:17.442 --> 21:19.695
Then how about your manager--

21:19.778 --> 21:21.780
I said I don't fucking have one.

21:21.863 --> 21:22.948
What's going on?

21:27.160 --> 21:29.538
Why are you swearing?
There are people around.

21:29.621 --> 21:32.249
So what if there are? Don't you swear?

21:32.332 --> 21:33.583
No, I don't.

21:34.376 --> 21:36.545
And I'm not a celebrity, unlike you.

21:37.337 --> 21:38.755
I'm not either. Not anymore.

21:46.388 --> 21:49.016
Ms. Lee Doona, is your guardian here?

21:50.809 --> 21:52.060
Ms. Lee Doona.

21:53.937 --> 21:55.022
I'm her guardian.

21:55.105 --> 21:56.857
You can talk to me.

21:56.940 --> 21:58.525
Could you please follow me?

22:04.197 --> 22:08.201
Thanks to your quick actions,
there are no particular complications,

22:08.285 --> 22:10.412
but her body temperature is
on the low side,

22:10.495 --> 22:14.624
so please make sure her head,
hands, and feet are always kept warm.

22:14.708 --> 22:17.419
A dry blanket will be useful here,

22:17.502 --> 22:19.796
and most importantly,
make sure she wears socks.

22:19.880 --> 22:23.175
Give her warm drinks
to help the recovery process.

22:23.258 --> 22:24.301
I see.

22:24.384 --> 22:27.929
Oh, and would there be
any other internal issues?

22:28.513 --> 22:30.599
Does she need any other tests?

22:30.682 --> 22:33.685
No, no further tests are needed.

22:33.769 --> 22:37.356
Oh, I'm sorry, but would you happen to
have a phone charger I could borrow?

22:37.439 --> 22:39.858
- I'll be one moment.
- Sure.

22:50.786 --> 22:52.120
They said to put socks on you.

22:54.790 --> 22:57.209
- So do it, then.
- Me?

22:58.251 --> 22:59.503
Aren't you my guardian?

23:11.056 --> 23:12.265
Excuse me.

23:28.865 --> 23:30.158
You'll have to excuse me.

23:39.334 --> 23:41.294
Weren't there any bed socks?

23:41.378 --> 23:42.254
I'm sorry?

23:42.337 --> 23:44.965
I mean, weren't there any ordinary ones?

23:45.048 --> 23:47.092
I like ordinary stuff.

23:49.428 --> 23:50.554
Are you laughing?

23:51.805 --> 23:52.681
No.

23:54.224 --> 23:58.061
It's just that you like ordinary stuff
when there's nothing ordinary about you.

23:59.980 --> 24:03.775
Bed socks can make your feet sweat
and end up making them colder.

24:03.859 --> 24:05.777
I got these on purpose.

24:05.861 --> 24:07.446
And at least they're pink.

24:07.529 --> 24:10.949
All the others looked like dad socks.
I chose these carefully.

24:21.376 --> 24:23.962
What's your name, Mr. Guardian?

24:24.045 --> 24:25.046
Me?

24:30.051 --> 24:32.095
That's personal information.

24:50.197 --> 24:52.616
KOOK SU-JIN

24:54.618 --> 24:55.869
Hey, Kooksu.

24:55.952 --> 24:58.205
Hey, do you smoke?

25:00.081 --> 25:01.124
Oh, smoke.

25:01.625 --> 25:02.667
What, me?

25:02.751 --> 25:06.379
My mom's friend says to tell you
not to come for the tutoring job.

25:08.048 --> 25:08.882
What?

25:08.965 --> 25:10.300
You jackass.

25:10.383 --> 25:13.845
She asked me three times to confirm
that you're a non-smoker, and I said yes.

25:13.929 --> 25:17.516
But then she found that your scarf
absolutely reeked of cigarette smoke!

25:30.862 --> 25:32.155
My 800,000 won.

25:32.864 --> 25:34.157
I can't believe this.

25:44.167 --> 25:46.753
YOUR ITEM HAS BEEN DELIVERED

25:58.473 --> 25:59.474
Won-jun.

26:03.853 --> 26:04.896
Have you had breakfast?

26:06.106 --> 26:07.524
If not, let's eat together.

26:08.650 --> 26:11.319
Is that my package by any chance?

26:20.036 --> 26:20.954
What is it?

26:21.037 --> 26:22.372
It's really cushy.

26:23.248 --> 26:25.542
Why would you sit
on someone else's package?

26:25.625 --> 26:27.002
I'm so hungry.

26:27.085 --> 26:28.545
What shall we eat?

26:28.628 --> 26:30.005
Have a nice day.

26:40.682 --> 26:44.269
That was the day
she started waiting for me.

26:51.318 --> 26:53.153
Won-jun, have you eaten?

26:53.236 --> 26:55.238
Shall we go for tteokbokki?

26:56.906 --> 26:57.824
Won-jun!

27:01.244 --> 27:02.704
Jokbal and bossam combo?

27:04.664 --> 27:05.999
Won-jun, let's go eat!

27:20.221 --> 27:21.765
This is seriously driving me nuts.

27:28.104 --> 27:29.356
Hello.

27:32.400 --> 27:33.234
Hello.

27:33.318 --> 27:36.613
If you're here to hang up your laundry,
do it. Don't mind me.

28:14.067 --> 28:17.153
My friend gave it to me
as a birthday present.

28:17.237 --> 28:19.322
But he wants it back,
so I'm gonna return it.

28:19.406 --> 28:21.783
I only wore it the other day
'cause it's fleece-lined.

28:21.866 --> 28:23.368
It was cold that day, right?

28:23.451 --> 28:24.369
Did I say anything?

28:24.452 --> 28:26.746
- No, but in case you got the wrong idea.
- I didn't.

28:26.830 --> 28:27.914
You said you're not a fan.

28:28.832 --> 28:29.999
So that means you're not.

28:39.092 --> 28:41.553
You dress well for an engineering major.

28:42.470 --> 28:44.055
Does your girlfriend choose your clothes?

28:44.764 --> 28:46.307
I don't have a girlfriend.

28:49.310 --> 28:50.645
I'm hungry.

28:50.729 --> 28:51.896
Shall we get something to eat?

28:54.691 --> 28:57.527
Actually, can I ask you something?

29:00.029 --> 29:00.864
Did you maybe…

29:02.824 --> 29:04.826
fall for me?

29:08.037 --> 29:09.330
Please don't do this.

29:10.039 --> 29:11.833
It's making me uncomfortable.

29:23.052 --> 29:24.637
Why are you laughing?

29:26.306 --> 29:28.183
You're so funny.

29:31.394 --> 29:33.897
I haven't laughed like this
in a long time.

29:36.900 --> 29:38.276
- Look.
- Yes?

29:38.359 --> 29:39.611
I won't fall for you.

29:39.694 --> 29:41.362
I'll never fall for you.

29:42.447 --> 29:44.407
"Never" is a bit unnecessary.

29:46.326 --> 29:47.202
Let's be friends.

29:48.161 --> 29:49.537
I want to be friends with you.

29:50.163 --> 29:52.540
With me? Why?

29:52.624 --> 29:54.125
Because I don't have any friends.

29:58.254 --> 30:01.591
The first floor is for girls.
Maybe you should make friends with them?

30:01.674 --> 30:04.344
First floor?
I have the whole floor to myself.

30:05.428 --> 30:06.888
Wow, you're rich.

30:06.971 --> 30:08.973
I suddenly want to be
best friends with you.

30:09.057 --> 30:10.809
Really? Does that mean I can call you?

30:10.892 --> 30:12.018
No.

30:12.101 --> 30:13.520
You're a tough nut to crack.

30:13.603 --> 30:14.729
Of course I am.

30:17.148 --> 30:18.525
It can't be helped, then.

30:19.025 --> 30:22.153
If I get attacked by a stalker and die,
it'll be your fault.

30:23.071 --> 30:24.614
Why would it be my fault?

30:24.697 --> 30:27.617
The sun's coming up. I have to make
a wish, so stop bothering me.

30:27.700 --> 30:29.369
When did I bother you?

31:31.014 --> 31:32.557
- Hey.
- Huh?

31:33.641 --> 31:34.851
You forgot your underpants.

31:48.489 --> 31:49.866
I wish I could move.

32:12.847 --> 32:14.140
Kim Jin-ju!

32:14.223 --> 32:15.099
Jju!

32:16.434 --> 32:17.435
Sorry we're late.

32:17.518 --> 32:18.394
Let's eat.

32:18.478 --> 32:19.312
Is it good?

32:26.736 --> 32:27.612
Lee Won-jun.

32:30.406 --> 32:31.240
Hey.

32:33.701 --> 32:36.996
Didn't you hear me calling you?
You can have this back.

32:37.080 --> 32:38.498
You can keep it on if you want.

32:38.581 --> 32:39.916
No. It smells of cigarette smoke.

32:45.505 --> 32:46.464
Let me.

32:58.768 --> 32:59.602
It's done.

33:02.814 --> 33:03.648
See you later.

33:04.273 --> 33:05.108
Yeah.

33:06.609 --> 33:08.236
- Who was that?
- What do you mean?

33:08.319 --> 33:10.863
- Who is he? Tell us.
- It's just someone I know.

33:10.947 --> 33:12.198
He's good-looking.

33:12.281 --> 33:14.617
What's with the vibe between you two?

33:14.701 --> 33:15.994
"Just someone I know."

33:20.289 --> 33:22.333
Can't you tell her I don't smoke?

33:22.917 --> 33:26.170
A friend, no, what am I saying?
I mean, some weirdo…

33:27.046 --> 33:28.548
Anyhow, it's not me.

33:30.550 --> 33:31.509
She's found someone?

33:32.552 --> 33:33.428
Already?

33:33.928 --> 33:35.888
That's ten in total. 70,000 won, please.

33:37.598 --> 33:38.558
Yes, thank you.

34:04.542 --> 34:07.336
PART-TIMERS WANTED
RECRUITING STAFF MEMBERS FOR CAFÉ 1890

34:09.172 --> 34:10.048
Hello.

34:13.676 --> 34:15.386
- Take it down.
- I'm sorry?

34:16.179 --> 34:17.221
I said take it down.

34:17.305 --> 34:19.432
Oh, aren't we allowed
to put things up here?

34:19.515 --> 34:22.894
You need to pay
to get this little stamp here.

34:22.977 --> 34:25.104
You think it's okay
to post things willy-nilly?

34:49.337 --> 34:51.422
Tutoring? That's a piece of cake!

34:51.506 --> 34:53.007
Ladies and gentlemen!

34:53.091 --> 34:54.467
The Brains of Yangjin!

34:54.550 --> 34:56.052
Yangjin born and bred!

34:56.135 --> 34:58.805
Lee Won-jun!

35:01.474 --> 35:03.267
- I'll visit often.
- What for?

35:03.351 --> 35:05.311
Don't forget to take the pumpkin juice.

35:05.394 --> 35:07.522
It's in the crisper drawer of the fridge.

35:08.940 --> 35:10.149
Won-jun!

35:11.651 --> 35:13.569
If you get a girlfriend, send photos!

35:13.653 --> 35:15.446
Go inside! It's cold!

35:15.530 --> 35:17.615
Make sure you take
your medication on time!

35:46.477 --> 35:47.353
Hello?

35:48.604 --> 35:49.730
Hello?

35:51.315 --> 35:53.860
I got your number from your flier.

35:54.610 --> 35:56.028
Yes, how can I help you?

35:56.112 --> 35:59.323
I was wondering if you would

36:00.783 --> 36:04.036
go out for a meal with me sometime.

36:21.971 --> 36:22.805
Are you angry?

36:23.890 --> 36:24.724
No.

36:24.807 --> 36:26.017
You are. I can tell.

36:26.601 --> 36:30.021
Hey, why don't you get mad at me?
I want to see you get mad.

36:30.521 --> 36:32.023
Why are you angry though?

36:32.106 --> 36:34.650
Didn't you stick them everywhere
so people would call?

36:36.027 --> 36:36.986
Look here.

36:38.154 --> 36:39.906
Are you that bored?

36:40.489 --> 36:41.949
Is this your idea of fun?

36:43.117 --> 36:45.494
You can do whatever you want
because you're a bum

36:45.578 --> 36:47.580
who's rolling in time and money.

36:47.663 --> 36:49.749
You don't care how you live your life.

36:49.832 --> 36:51.167
Well, congratulations.

36:51.792 --> 36:54.837
But you know what?
Not everyone can live like that.

36:54.921 --> 36:57.798
I desperately need a job.
I also need to study.

36:58.507 --> 37:00.968
I have a lot on my plate at the moment.

37:01.052 --> 37:03.221
So please, for the love of God,

37:03.304 --> 37:05.806
stop following me
and playing pranks on me.

37:07.058 --> 37:10.436
I don't find them amusing
in the slightest.

37:13.856 --> 37:17.318
Well, now that I've seen it,
I'm really disappointed.

37:17.902 --> 37:19.153
I see you have no talent

37:20.112 --> 37:21.197
for getting mad.

37:21.697 --> 37:23.950
I understand what you're saying.

38:49.535 --> 38:50.411
Hello?

38:57.335 --> 38:58.377
Ms. Lee?

39:01.005 --> 39:02.882
Let's go out for a meal sometime.

39:03.883 --> 39:05.301
Whenever you want.

39:05.926 --> 39:07.011
It'll be my treat.

39:09.013 --> 39:10.556
As soon as I find a tutoring job.

39:16.020 --> 39:17.021
Oh my god!

39:33.662 --> 39:36.540
The presumed value of Vb
is pointing downward,

39:36.624 --> 39:38.834
so we calculate it as a negative value.

39:38.918 --> 39:42.004
Under the condition
that the aggregate force equals zero,

39:42.088 --> 39:45.549
Vb comes out to 75 newtons.

39:45.633 --> 39:47.968
Now, we'll move on to the bending moment.

39:48.052 --> 39:50.596
We need to calculate
the aggregate bending moment

39:50.679 --> 39:51.806
that applies to point B.

39:51.889 --> 39:53.974
Under the condition
of the equilibrium equation,

39:54.058 --> 39:56.310
the aggregate bending moment
at point B is zero.

39:56.394 --> 39:58.938
Positive direction means
a clockwise direction.

39:59.021 --> 40:02.566
Let's look at all the bending moments
that are being applied to point B.

40:02.650 --> 40:05.444
The reaction force of 120 newtons
applying to point A

40:05.528 --> 40:08.823
is rotating in a clockwise direction
in relation to point B.

40:16.330 --> 40:17.164
Let's go eat.

40:17.248 --> 40:18.207
Now?

40:18.290 --> 40:19.500
You said whenever I want.

40:20.501 --> 40:21.919
I want to now.

40:31.887 --> 40:32.721
For now,

40:33.639 --> 40:36.225
I think we need to wait
until class is over.

40:42.106 --> 40:43.274
What should we eat?

41:06.005 --> 41:07.798
Don't you mind being recognized?

41:07.882 --> 41:08.757
No.

41:09.508 --> 41:12.595
When I'm dressed like this,
not many people recognize me anyway.

41:14.138 --> 41:15.389
You didn't either.

41:16.182 --> 41:19.226
Actually, that was because
it felt so divorced from reality.

41:26.942 --> 41:27.776
I'll call you.

41:29.361 --> 41:30.404
You don't mind, do you?

41:30.988 --> 41:32.114
Well,

41:32.907 --> 41:34.033
if it's urgent.

41:50.883 --> 41:53.135
I'm telling you this just in case,

41:54.053 --> 41:55.846
but don't fall for me either.

41:56.347 --> 41:57.181
Me?

41:58.349 --> 42:00.809
I don't think there's any danger of that.

42:03.771 --> 42:04.980
You never know.

42:11.028 --> 42:15.074
Every life has its unexpected twists.

42:24.333 --> 42:25.626
You once said to me

42:26.669 --> 42:29.838
that you and I are
from different universes.

42:40.599 --> 42:43.644
That though we had been living
in completely different universes…

43:12.006 --> 43:18.012
we found ourselves sitting side by side
at the same station purely by chance.

43:30.774 --> 43:31.609
RECENT CALLS

43:33.986 --> 43:36.071
LEE

43:36.155 --> 43:37.698
DOONA

43:40.951 --> 43:42.995
Even though you may be right…

43:56.592 --> 43:57.551
I was happy…

44:01.138 --> 44:02.598
that it was you.
